\begin_layout Section
Model layers
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\begin_inset CommandInset label
LatexCommand label
name "sec:layers"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The model is built in three layers. Each layer assumes the layers below it are present, and adds a distinct kind of content: the accounting core adds book-keeping, the macroeconomic core adds optimising behaviour, and the green transition core adds physical energy and emissions. Satellite modules attach to the layers and are individually optional.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The point of the layering is that each layer is separately useful and separately testable. The accounting core contains no behavioural assumptions at all, so it can be run against a dataset on its own: if the data are internally inconsistent – if shares do not sum to one, or supply does not match use – the core fails to solve, and it fails in a way that identifies the offending cell. Adding the macroeconomic core turns the same accounting identities into a closed general-equilibrium model; adding the green transition core attaches physical energy quantities and emissions to those flows.
\end_layout

